data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = SubstrateInputsOnly

// THE SUBJECT IS THE CANDIDATE FIELD OF A REAL SPILL POPULATION, AND THE POPULATION IS UNEVEN ON
// PURPOSE BECAUSE THE REAL ONE IS.
//
// The CI spill roster names four compute offers - a Scaleway AMP2 instance, a Hetzner CAX41, an
// Oracle Ampere A1 and a GCP N2 on-demand instance. Exactly one of those four providers has a route
// whose data paths anybody has modeled. Three do not, and the question this file answers is what
// happens to the other three: whether an offer whose provider we have never assessed is refused,
// or whether it quietly reaches the ranking and wins on price because nothing was there to stop it.
//
// WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT ASSERT ABOUT ANY REAL VENDOR, stated first because getting this wrong is
// worse than the coverage gap it would paper over. The four offer IDENTITIES are real - those are
// products that exist and that our own spill roster names. THE ROUTE FACTS BELOW ARE NOT A READING
// OF ANY VENDOR'S SUBPROCESSOR DOCUMENTATION, DATA-RESIDENCY REPRESENTATIONS OR CONTRACT. They are
// this witness's declared inputs, and every one of them cites a row in this module that says so in
// its own text. DESIGN section 4d's rule is that a figure carries its evidentiary standing in the
// type rather than in a reader's memory; the standing of everything here is "witness input, read
// obligation outstanding", and the obligation is named. Nobody may cite this file as evidence that
// Hetzner's execution path is located where this file puts it - the whole point of the file is that
// the corpus has not read those paths for three of four providers, and it has not properly read
// them for the fourth either.
//
// WHY THE ONE MODELED ROUTE IS ALSO THE DEAREST. Scaleway is priced lowest and Hetzner highest, so
// the surviving offer is the one that loses on every economic axis. If compliance were a conjunct
// beside cost - or a tiebreak, or a penalty added to a total - the cheap unassessed offer would win
// and this file would go red. It wins nothing, because it is never in the list the ranker is
// handed.
//
// THE PRICES ARE ORDINALS, NOT QUOTES. They are 1000, 2000, 3000 and 4000 micros an hour, spaced so
// the ORDER is unmistakable and so no reader can mistake them for a vendor's published rate. The
// subject of every claim below is which offer survives, never what anything costs; a real quote
// belongs to a pricing authority and is cited from there, never transcribed into a witness.

// ── THE POPULATION'S ROUTE COMPONENTS, DECLARED SO EVERY CITATION RESOLVES ────────────────────
//
// The provider and service components of the Hetzner route cite extdeps.cloud.hetzner, which is the
// real upstream authority for that vendor and already carries its catalog. The REGION component
// cites a row in this module instead, and the reason is a real modeling state rather than laziness:
// that module models regions as a closed coproduct (HetznerCloudRegion = Helsinki | Nuremberg) with
// no per-region DECLARATION to name, and DESIGN section 3 requires citing a symbol rather than a
// position, so there is presently nothing upstream to point at. TRIGGER: a per-region declaration in
// extdeps.cloud.hetzner, at which point this row is deleted and the citation moves upstream.
data spill_hetzner_helsinki_region: NonEmptyStr = "Hetzner Cloud region Helsinki (hel1), named here because extdeps.cloud.hetzner models its regions as coproduct arms rather than as one declaration per region."
data spill_hetzner_nuremberg_region: NonEmptyStr = "Hetzner Cloud region Nuremberg (nbg1), the sibling region used by the route-mismatch red below."

// The three providers with no modeled route. These rows exist so the OFFERS can name the route they
// claim to run on - an offer must state its route or the facts row could never be found to disagree
// with it - and they deliberately carry NO facts. That is the population's actual state.
data spill_scaleway_provider: NonEmptyStr = "Scaleway SAS. NO ROUTE FACTS ARE MODELED FOR THIS PROVIDER in this corpus: no data-path closure, no downstream population, no contract terms. This row names the provider so an offer can cite it; it establishes nothing about the provider."
data spill_scaleway_service: NonEmptyStr = "Scaleway Elastic Metal / Instances AMP2 line, named for the offer identity only."
data spill_scaleway_region: NonEmptyStr = "Scaleway region as named by the spill roster, unread."
data spill_oracle_provider: NonEmptyStr = "Oracle Corporation (OCI). NO ROUTE FACTS ARE MODELED FOR THIS PROVIDER in this corpus."
data spill_oracle_service: NonEmptyStr = "OCI Compute Ampere A1 shape, named for the offer identity only."
data spill_oracle_region: NonEmptyStr = "OCI region as named by the spill roster, unread."
data spill_google_provider: NonEmptyStr = "Google LLC (Google Cloud). NO ROUTE FACTS ARE MODELED FOR THIS PROVIDER in this corpus."
data spill_google_service: NonEmptyStr = "Google Compute Engine N2 on-demand, named for the offer identity only."
data spill_google_region: NonEmptyStr = "GCP region as named by the spill roster, unread."

// ── THE WITNESS'S DECLARED INPUTS, EACH CARRYING ITS OWN STANDING ─────────────────────────────
data spill_witness_read_obligation: NonEmptyStr = "OUTSTANDING READ. Nobody in this corpus has read this provider's data-path closure - execution, durable storage, backups, logs, telemetry, control plane, support access, administrative access and spill - nor enumerated its downstream providers. Until that read lands and is cited to the provider's own published representations, every path standing in this witness is an INPUT TO A TEST and is not a fact about the provider."
data spill_witness_operator: NonEmptyStr = "The operating entity a located path names. Witness input; see spill_witness_read_obligation."
data spill_witness_jurisdiction: NonEmptyStr = "The jurisdiction a located path names. Witness input; see spill_witness_read_obligation."
data spill_witness_no_spill_path: NonEmptyStr = "A spill path declared absent. Witness input; see spill_witness_read_obligation."
data spill_witness_no_downstream: NonEmptyStr = "A downstream provider population declared empty. Witness input; see spill_witness_read_obligation."
data spill_witness_contract_terms: NonEmptyStr = "The agreement a route's facts row cites. Witness input; see spill_witness_read_obligation."
data spill_witness_posture_authority: NonEmptyStr = "The authority whose compliance posture revision this witness evaluates against. Witness input; see spill_witness_read_obligation."
data spill_witness_customer_profile: NonEmptyStr = "The customer profile the use is admitted for. Witness input."
data spill_witness_data_handling_profile: NonEmptyStr = "The data-handling profile the use is admitted for. Witness input."
data spill_witness_agreement: NonEmptyStr = "The agreement the sanction requires and the scope brings. Witness input."
data spill_witness_prohibited_use_cleared: NonEmptyStr = "Prohibited-use program clearance. Witness input."
data spill_witness_sanctions_cleared: NonEmptyStr = "Sanctions program clearance. Witness input."
data spill_witness_export_cleared: NonEmptyStr = "Export program clearance. Witness input."
data spill_witness_decision_receipt: NonEmptyStr = "The receipt the admission decision is recorded against. Witness input."

fn s_hash(seed: String) -> ContentHash {
  as_content_hash_structural(structural: content_hash_atom(value: seed))
}

